.\n\n---\n\n**Frames Featuring Characters Emerging from or Inside Gourds:**\n\n*   **Frame 6:** This frame shows a close-up of a character's lower body and head. The character has a long, pointed snout, red scales, and is wearing a blue skirt with a red bow. This is the Snake Demon, a villainous character. She is not emerging from a gourd; she is simply shown in a close-up, likely after having been introduced or having moved into the scene. **No character is emerging from a gourd in this frame.**\n\n*   **Frame 26:** This frame shows a close-up of a large, purple, frog-like creature with a wide, open mouth and red eyes. This is the Toad Demon, another villain. He is inside a circular, ornate frame, possibly a mirror or a magical portal, but he is not emerging from a calabash gourd. **No character is emerging from a gourd in this frame.**\n\n*   **Frame 27:** This frame shows a magical, diamond-shaped crystal or mirror. Inside this crystal, a scene is reflected: the elderly man is kneeling on the ground, holding a hoe, and tending to the vine of calabash gourds. A red rooster stands nearby. This is a reflection of the earlier scenes, not a character emerging from a gourd. **No character is emerging from a gourd in this frame.**\n\n---\n\n**Regarding the Second Calabash Boy:**\n\nAfter carefully reviewing all 30 frames, **there is no scene depicted where the second Calabash Boy (or any of the other Calabash Brothers) emerges from a calabash gourd.**\n\nThe frames show the elderly man interacting with the gourds, holding them, and looking at them with care and anticipation. The gourds are shown hanging on the vine, and the villains (Snake Demon, Toad Demon) are shown in separate scenes, but none of the frames capture the actual moment of a Calabash Brother being born or emerging from his gourd. The video segment provided focuses on the setup and the villains, not the birth of the heroes."}, {'batch_start': 120, 'batch_end': 150, 'image_paths': ['/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/v